  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#42401\", \"PowerToys#46461\", \"PowerToys#47986\"], \"answer\": \"This feature has been requested before, and Light Switch can't do it yet. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#42401, 'Auto changing desktop background image alongside with Light switch'. Other requests for the same thing, such as #46461 and #45559, were closed as duplicates of it. #47986 was closed as a duplicate of #42413 ('Select specific light/dark themes'), which would switch whole Windows theme files including the wallpaper. Add a thumbs-up or a comment on #42401 to show interest. Until it's built, you can set the wallpaper in one of these ways. First, use a Windows theme or a task scheduler task that changes the wallpaper. Second, use a third-party tool such as Auto Dark Mode, which can switch wallpapers with the theme. Third, if you use Wallpaper Engine, use its command-line options.\"}",
